Note (transparency, no red-as-green): the instrumented androidTest source set is NOT part of this gate
(assembleRelease + testReleaseUnitTest do not compile androidTest). OfflineBannerUiTest.kt is authored
correctly - it calls .assertDoesNotExist() as a SemanticsNodeInteraction member (no import) and imports only
top-level assertions (assertIsDisplayed / assertHasClickAction / onNodeWithTag / onNodeWithText), mirroring the
known-good ServiceStatusUiTest. A whole-source-set compileDebugAndroidTestKotlin was run as an extra check: it
fails ONLY on pre-existing, out-of-scope sibling files (~23 files e.g. EnergyStatsWidgetUiTest,
KioskSettingsModal, FSMStateDiagramUiTest, AnnotationListUiTest) that wrongly import
assertDoesNotExist/assertExists/onAllNodes as top-level symbols; ZERO errors mention OfflineBannerUiTest. Those
files are outside this prompt's allowed paths and were not modified.

Binding note: web OfflineBanner.tsx's only data source is useOnlineStatus (navigator.onLine + the resilience
status broadcaster), which has no KMP observer, and this surface may not add one. The surface binds the one
wired cross-cutting service-reachability signal - the ADR-009 live pipeline (LiveSessionStore, the same feed
LiveIndicator / ServiceStatus bind) - and maps the live wire health onto the web online/offline branches:
Disconnected -> Offline (web-verbatim pwa.offline.title / pwa.offline.banner + WifiOff + reconnect),
Reconnecting -> Reconnecting (honest "Reconnecting..." heading + the cached-data body),
Connected / Unknown(cold start) -> Online dormant (faithful web `if (online) return null`). The banner is a
polite live region (web role="status" / aria-live="polite"). Disclosed here, not dressed up as a
navigator.onLine read.

